{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>וירח</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: וירח את ריח בגדיו. And this is what the Sages of blessed memory expounded: even the transgressors of Israel are destined to give off fragrance, and this is it: וירח את ריח בגדיו — do not read בגדיו but בוגדיו. And וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח — that they are destined to give the fragrance of ניחוח. Another interpretation: a hint that the fragrance of Gan Eden entered with him when he smelled the fragrance of his garments, then וירח ה׳:" "<b>מנעריו</b> Three times in the Masorah: here and the others: איש מלחמה מנעוריו. שאנן מואב מנעוריו. From his youth a person must do battle with the evil inclination, and if he overcomes it and defeats it — שאנן מואב מנעוריו — and he is tranquil, at rest upon his watch:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:52.423652453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}